WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.040
As Hollywood gears up for the 2018 blockbuster
season, movie studios are throwing out new

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.950
trailers right and left.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:12.219
February alone saw new glimpses of Infinity
War, Deadpool 2, Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom,

00:00:12.219 --> 00:00:13.799
and so much more.

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:17.580
It's hard to keep track of everything that's
worth watching, so we rounded up the best

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.040
February movie trailers that are sure to blow
you away.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.620
"Oh, wow. That was unrealistically fast. Okay, hit it."

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.150
The Hurricane Heist

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:33.710
The ultimate storm meets the perfect heist
in The Hurricane Heist, an action extravaganza

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.550
about a group of thieves who plan to rob the
U.S. Treasury in the middle of a category

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.969
five hurricane.

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:43.160
Appropriately, The Scorpions' "Rock You Like
a Hurricane" forms the musical backdrop to

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.350
a crazy montage of thievery and stormy weather.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:52.710
"Just say here and let's consider the word
to be short for "here I am, rock you like

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.710
a hurricane."

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.760
"You do as the Scorpions have before you!"

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.210
Coming from director Rob Cohen of xXx and
The Fast and the Furious, it's bound to be

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.960
an action-packed ride.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.899
Look for it on March 9th.

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:05.250
The Outsider

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:10.280
Jared Leto is in top form in the trailer for
The Outsider, a Netflix film that will be

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.010
arriving in early March.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.549
Leto plays Nick Lowell, an American soldier
held captive in Japan at the end of World

00:01:16.549 --> 00:01:17.549
War II.

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:22.450
In exchange for his freedom, he has to join
the yakuza and adopt their way of life, no

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.780
matter how much blood he has to shed.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.070
Take a look on March 9th.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.070
Gringo

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:33.930
Amazon Studios dropped the final trailer for
their dark comedy Gringo in February, adding

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:38.250
even more excitement to what already looked
like a funny, action-filled tale.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.970
Representing a U.S. medical company, a naive
businessman travels to a factory in Mexico

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.659
to deliver the formula for a new high-tech
cannabis pill.

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:50.170
Unfortunately, he also becomes a target for
a drug cartel.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.979
Wacky, murderous hijinks ensue.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:59.420
Gringo stars David Oyelowo, Joel Edgerton,
and Charlize Theron, and premieres on March

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.420
9th.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.479
Pacific Rim: Uprising

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:07.159
Even though Guillermo del Toro isn't returning
to helm Pacific Rim: Uprising, the trailers

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.690
so far at least have us hoping that it'll
preserve the magic of the first film.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.700
That is to say, it better be mostly about
giant robots duking it out with giant monsters.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.940
"That's what I'm talking about."

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.210
With February's IMAX trailer, it's looking
more and more like the filmmakers behind Pacific

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:26.410
Rim: Uprising understand what made its predecessor
cheesy and wonderful.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:32.330
It's full of useless inspirational speeches,
people shouting, and robots with swords.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.160
One of the Kaiju gets a Mechagodzilla upgrade.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.020
This is all good stuff.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:41.260
As long as the movie doesn't try to make us
care too much about Stacker's son, consider

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.440
us pumped.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.130
Check it out on March 23rd.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.540
Ready Player One

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.220
For a movie that's mostly going to be a giant
game of spot the nostalgia, Ready Player One

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.220
is starting to look like one of the most visually
interesting blockbusters of the year.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.780
Two trailers for the movie were released in
February.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.920
The first shows more general footage, but
the second reveals the basic plotline for

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.610
those who don't already know it.

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:08.520
A voiceover explains that there are three
keys that open three gates, and whoever finds

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.350
them all wins a prize.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:15.140
That prize is trillions of dollars left behind
by the creator of the virtual reality world

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:20.170
OASIS, and the entire story is about one kid
trying to find all the keys before anyone

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.170
else.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.420
Look for it on March 29th.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.790
The Titan

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:29.170
Starring Sam Worthington as a soldier selected
to become one of the first humans on Titan,

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:33.830
Saturn's largest moon, The Titan looks like
a sleek action sci-fi experience.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:38.200
In the trailer, we see Worthington's character
undergo a genetic experiment that transforms

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:43.400
him into a freaky, white-skinned monster — clearly,
there were a few unintended side effects.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.360
The Titan will premiere on Netflix on March
30th, so you won't even have to leave the

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.870
house for this one.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.760
The Last Movie Star

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:55.010
Burt Reynolds headlines The Last Movie Star
as an aging actor who's being honored with

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.060
a lifetime achievement award.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.500
What he doesn't know is that the award is
being presented in a run-down bar in Tennessee.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.940
"Let's get you over to the red carpet."

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.930
The experience prompts him to go on a journey
of self-discovery.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:13.040
It looks like an emotional film with one of
the best actors of the generation, and well

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.540
worth checking out on March 30.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.350
A Quiet Place

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:22.820
After cutting his directing teeth on the 2016
romcom The Hollars, John Krasinski is back

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.690
behind the camera for A Quiet Place, a unique
twist on the horror genre about mysterious

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:30.620
monsters that hunt down anyone they can hear.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:35.030
Krasinski and Emily Blunt star as two parents
trying to keep their family safe in this freaky

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.280
new world.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:40.320
The trailer doesn't reveal much beyond the
initial setup, although we know that the creatures

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:45.250
came via some kind of invasion and Emily Blunt's
character is pregnant, which is bound to lead

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.400
to a tense childbirth scene.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.760
Find out on April 6th.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.220
10x10

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.890
For the true romantics out there, there's
nothing like a little kidnapping to get you

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.790
in the mood for Valentine's Day.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:01.210
Released on February 13th, this trailer sees
Luke Evans starring as a man who abducts a

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.140
woman and locks her in a padded room in his
house.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:08.230
His motives are unclear, but the trailer hints
that there may be a deeper connection between

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.230
these two people.

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.230
"Why are you doing this?

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.380
I think you already know."

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:17.501
10x10 looks like a thrilling psychological
study, and a welcome change of pace as we

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:19.480
head into blockbuster season.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.880
Look for it on April 13th.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.530
Marrowbone

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:27.350
If a horror trailer that isn't jammed full
of jump scares sounds like an interesting

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.170
twist, you'll definitely want to check out
the trailer for Marrowbone.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:35.340
Four recently orphaned children hide out in
their family's abandoned estate to keep the

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:40.840
state from separating them, only to find out
that the crumbling house may actually be haunted.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:45.130
It's The Boxcar Children crossed with The
Shining, and it features a fantastic cast

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:51.180
of up-and-coming actors, including Stranger
Things' Charlie Heaton, Split's Anya Taylor-Joy,

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:54.030
and Captain Fantastic's George MacKay.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.639
Experience all the thrills on April 13th.

00:05:56.639 --> 00:05:58.380
Rampage

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:03.460
Starring Dwayne Johnson, Jeffrey Dean Morgan,
and lots of CGI, Rampage is bound to be the

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.750
year's biggest movie about giant fighting
monsters that isn't Pacific Rim.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:12.180
Judging by the trailer, it's going to be a
pretty faithful adaptation of the 1986 arcade

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.770
game, plus bonus material in the form of all
the human characters and the whole "story"

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:17.770
part.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.820
At least the three main characters are all
present — George, the enormous gorilla;

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:27.200
Lizzie, the Godzilla thing; and Ralph, the
radioactive wolf who can fly if he eats the

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.570
right toxic sludge.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.330
"Of course the wolf flies."

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.400
Rampage will be tearing up the box office
on April 20th.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.270
Batman Ninja

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:40.780
DC's cinematic universe may leave a lot to
be desired, but the company has always made

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:45.530
solid animated films, and Batman Ninja looks
like another amazing entry.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:50.840
A freak energy surge sends Batman back in
time to feudal Japan — along with a ton

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:56.360
of villains, including the Joker, Harley Quinn,
Deathstroke, and Gorilla Grodd.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:00.960
Batman will have to stop them from rewriting
history if he wants to save the future.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.520
Yeah, it sounds as awesome as it looks.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.169
Look for it on streaming sites on April 24th.

00:07:06.169 --> 00:07:08.480
Avengers: Infinity War

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:12.960
At this point, there's no way the hype for
Infinity War can get any bigger, but the newly

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.870
released Super Bowl trailer definitely makes
a bid to change that.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:21.180
Featuring even more shots of Earth's Mightiest
Heroes and their franchise pals preparing

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:26.070
for war against Thanos, the entire trailer
is tailor-made to make fans' hearts pound.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:27.070
"Let's go."

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.070
Not that we're complaining.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:31.930
We'll take every piece of Infinity War footage
Marvel wants to give us leading up to the

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:34.200
film's May 4th release.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.080
Deadpool 2

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:40.710
Hands down the most hilarious trailer from
February is the "Deadpool, Meet Cable" trailer

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:42.200
for Deadpool 2.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.020
While it starts out like a typical teaser,
it switches gears just a few seconds in and

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:49.000
becomes much more, well, Deadpool.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.330
"Wait, no, stop.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.790
What in the actual ass?"

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:58.520
So Wade takes matters into his own hands and
stages his own action-packed reveal with Cable

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.590
and Deadpool action figures.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:04.430
After that bit, however, the trailer picks
up again, giving fans their first look at

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:06.730
Cable in action, and it's amazing.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:11.180
We're also given glimpses of some of the new
mutants taking on the shadowy DMC.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.490
And of course, all the familiar faces are
back.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:17.260
It'll be hard to top the first movie, but
judging by this trailer, it just may happen

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.830
on May 18th.

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.070
Solo: A Star Wars Story

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:25.590
The first teaser trailer for Solo: A Star
Wars Story was met with mixed reactions.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:29.990
Some fans are looking forward to seeing Alden
Ehrenreich stepping in as a young Han Solo,

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.240
while others were left saying:

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.529
"I got a bad feeling about this…"

00:08:34.529 --> 00:08:38.470
Filled with in-jokes from the original films
and cloying glimpses of everything from the

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:43.150
Millenium Falcon to Donald Glover's Lando,
the trailer is definitely a treat for the

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:44.150
eyes.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:49.430
Whether the film itself leaves the same impression
remains to be seen on May 25th.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:50.850
Incredibles 2

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:55.380
It's been 14 long years since The Incredibles
first hit theaters, so you better believe

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.830
the release of the Incredibles 2 trailer was
an earth-shattering event — and not just

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.850
because The Underminer is back.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.260
Fortunately, it looks like it was worth the
wait.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:08.860
The trailer focuses on Mr. Incredible staying
home with the kids while Elastigirl goes off

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:13.190
on a mission, leading to all the jokes you
could ask for involving a stay-at-home dad

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.280
with unruly superpowered kids.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.560
"But I can't keep giving him cookies.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.250
No biting daddy!"

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.520
Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:27.150
While the first trailer offered a glimpse
of Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom back in

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:32.529
2017, the newly released trailer is bigger,
bolder, and more Jurassic.

00:09:32.529 --> 00:09:37.260
When a dormant volcano on Jurassic World threatens
to erupt, Owen and Claire head back to the

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.830
island to rescue their prehistoric friends.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:44.770
But dinosaurs will be dinosaurs, those silly
goofs, so they're still set on eating Owen

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.140
and Claire and everybody else made of meat.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.480
"You need to get us out of here."

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:54.830
Will the heroic duo be able to save the dinosaurs
before it's too late?

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:58.860
And more importantly, will saving them put
the rest of the world in danger?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.350
We'll find out on June 22nd.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:02.420
Skyscraper

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:07.480
The only things bigger than Dwayne Johnson's
biceps are the movies he's starring in these

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:08.480
days.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:13.240
Skyscraper marks yet another high-octane blockbuster
release for Johnson in 2018, and it's filled

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:18.630
with enough machine guns, explosions, and
gravity-defying antics to get any action fan

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.630
excited.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:21.290
Take the plunge on July 13th.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:23.850
Mission: Impossible — Fallout

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:28.260
Counter to the way most franchises operate,
the Mission: Impossible series just keeps

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.330
getting better.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:33.940
This time, Ethan Hunt and his gang of spies
have to deal with some kind of nuclear threat,

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.460
and Hunt may have been betrayed...again.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:41.250
But where the trailer plays coy on plot reveals,
it revels in its own self-awareness and glorious

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:45.610
stunts — like stealing a helicopter in mid-air
and doing a barrel roll.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:48.200
Which, per Cruise tradition, all actually
happened.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.570
"Same old Ethan."

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:53.390
And that wasn't even the craziest stunt Tom
Cruise pulled for the movie.

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:55.000
"I knew I broke it instantly."

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.000
"Two down."

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.120
"Well anyone else would go, well that's over,
NO.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.120
Up he gets, and he's running!"

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.940
He just runs away on a broken foot, gotta
catch those bad guys.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:12.370
Superman is literally in the movie, and Tom
Cruise still manages to out-Superman him.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.750
Give this madman an Oscar already.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.560
Venom

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.930
The internet spent a solid year champing at
the bit for their first glimpse of Tom Hardy

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:24.410
as Venom, and now...well, we're still waiting.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:29.370
Despite not actually showing Venom, the film's
first trailer does introduce Hardy's character,

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:34.399
Eddie Brock, in his human form, apparently
after an accident that landed him in the hospital.

00:11:34.399 --> 00:11:38.940
From there, we see a few vague action scenes
and a brief glimpse of something black and

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:43.610
symbiote-y writhing in a tank — before the
trailer takes us back to hospitalized Hardy

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.839
freaking out while a few black veins creep
up his neck.

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:50.640
Honestly, we could have waited another month
for a better trailer, but this one did the

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.770
job of whetting our appetite for the eventual
big reveal.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.890
Which...will come, right?

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:56.890
Eventually?

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.420
Hopefully, before the movie's October 5th
release.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:00.839
Thanks for watching!

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:03.490
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.459
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

